    "open_questions": [
      "Dancin' Fool's verses and the bars that change meter: only a machine tab exists; Bishop transcribed the opening, the break and the yowza interlude.",
      "U.K.'s Danger Money (The Only Thing She Needs in 5/4 and the rest): only machine tabs, whose meters and tempo map do not fit the record; not scored.",
      "The Black Page #1 and #2: nested tuplets in thirty-seconds and sixty-fourths that one level of tuplet on a sixteenth grid cannot hold.",
      "His solo ostinato pieces: the melody on tuned toms is the point, and the grid has no pitch.",
      "Jeff Beck's Guitar Shop (1989): no human drum tab found.",
      "The kit he played with Zappa (make and sizes): only the Rototoms (Bishop) and the black shells seen in Baby Snakes."
    ]
  },
